  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday night through next Tuesday)\nIssued at 144 PM CST Tue Nov 24 2026\n\nA much drier pattern should set up for the rest of the holiday week \nand through this weekend.  Another calm, clear night is expected for \nWednesday night so temperatures will drop down to around freezing \nagain.  For Turkey Day, surface high pressure will remain in control \nacross Texas so high temperatures will be in the mid 50s again. \nStarting Thursday night and continuing through the weekend, there \nwill be a gradual warmup as the cold surface high pressure moves \neastward to the Gulf coast and warm southerly return flow resumes. \nHigh temperatures look to climb back into the 60s and 70s while low \ntemperatures will be in the upper 30s to mid 40s.  Global models \ncurrently show one or two weak cold fronts intruding into west \ncentral Texas for Sunday into Monday.  However, at this point, \nprecipitation chances are low (<10%) and temperatures should not be \naffected.",
